> I love playing doppelgangers in Slash'em. That, however, does not
> translate into playing doppelgangers *well* in slash'em, so I'd like
> to devote a thread to cute doppelganger techniques. To start things
> off,

> 1. poly into Xorn and raid vaults.
> Pro: great way to explore, immunity to footrices ("you enter a
> disgusting nest!" is a common message in Slash'em), lots of gems!
>
> Con: you'd *better* have a wand or ring of polymorph or scroll of
> teleportation in case you get stuck in a wall.

Alsor aid shops where you don't intend to come back (minetown and Sam are  
favourite) or at a time where you'll be able to manage the shopkeeper or  
if you don't intend to spend much time here in the way back (Mall,  
typically).

> 3. turn into a cockatrice to lay eggs/"stoning grenades".
> The obvious downside is the -2 luck penalty for breaking your own
> eggs. Like they say, the devteam thinks of everything.

Basilisk are better since you can also keep a few eggs for hatching and a  
handful of powerful statue maker.
And -2 luck for instakilling the big D is something I'm willing to pay  
every day. (turn into a basilisk and let him instakill himself while  
hitting you)

Don't forget the "turn into crystal golem and get all intrinsic you need  
plus some more".
Of course, all the "turn into a metalivore and eat ring" and similar  
tricks are always nice.

The liquid leap technique is also quite usueful in certain Sokoban levels  
where there are iron bars between the entry and a convenient spot near the  
exit.

And if you can manage to train the puppies, polymorphing into a dragon and  
lay eggs can also be a lot of fun.
[especially if, like me, you play the the "pet ranged attack" patch  
allowing them to use breath weapon...]


Of course with doppelgangers an early wish usually goes to amulet of  
unchanging rather than usual DSM... Then you don't care about being stuck  
in walls or turning back to human from crystal golem in front of Vecna...

